{
  "id": "b1.g10", "level": "B1", "kind": "grammar",
  "title": "Separable and prefix verbs",
  "subtitle": "One verb in every position, prefix families, and stress that changes the meaning",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "b1.g10.l1", "title": "One separable verb, every position", "kind": "grammar",
      "explain": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "A **separable verb** has a stressed prefix (*op-, mee-, uit-, terug-, aan-, af-, in-*). Where the prefix stands depends on the sentence. In a **main clause** with a single verb the prefix goes to the **end**. In a **subordinate clause**, after a **modal**, or in the **infinitive** the verb stays in **one piece**. In the **perfect** the participle gets **ge-** between prefix and verb. With **te** the *te* goes in the middle." },
        { "type": "table", "head": ["position", "opbellen", "meenemen"], "rows": [["present", "Ik bel je op.", "Zij neemt een paraplu mee."], ["past", "Ik belde je op.", "Zij nam een paraplu mee."], ["perfect", "Ik heb je opgebeld.", "Zij heeft een paraplu meegenomen."], ["after a modal", "Ik wil je opbellen.", "Zij moet een paraplu meenemen."], ["subordinate clause", "…dat ik je opbel.", "…dat zij een paraplu meeneemt."], ["with te", "…om je op te bellen.", "…een paraplu mee te nemen."]] },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Ik bel je morgen op.", "en": "I will call you tomorrow." },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Ik probeer haar vandaag op te bellen.", "en": "I am trying to call her today." },
        { "type": "tip", "text": "More forms: *uitnodigen* – nodigt uit, nodigde uit, heeft **uitgenodigd**, **uit te nodigen**. *terugkomen* – komt terug, kwam terug, is **teruggekomen**, **terug te komen**." }
      ],
      "items": [
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik ___ je morgen op.", "options": ["bel", "bellen", "opbel"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Gisteren ___ hij zijn vriend op. (past tense)", "options": ["belde", "opbelde", "belden"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Hij heeft zijn vriend ___.", "options": ["opgebeld", "geopbeld", "gebeld op"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik hoop dat hij me morgen ___.", "options": ["opbelt", "belt op", "op belt"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Vergeet niet haar morgen ___!", "options": ["op te bellen", "te opbellen", "opte bellen"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Zij ___ om tien uur aan. (aankomen)", "answers": ["komt"], "en": "She arrives at ten o'clock." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Wij ___ onze vrienden gisteren uit. (uitnodigen, past)", "answers": ["nodigden"], "en": "We invited our friends yesterday." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Hij is gisteren ___. (terugkomen)", "answers": ["teruggekomen"], "en": "He came back yesterday." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik heb mijn paraplu ___. (meenemen)", "answers": ["meegenomen"], "en": "I have taken my umbrella with me." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik heb het formulier ___. (invullen)", "answers": ["ingevuld"], "en": "I have filled in the form." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik weet dat hij je morgen ___. (opbellen)", "answers": ["opbelt"], "en": "I know that he will call you tomorrow." },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik bel hem op.", "instruction": "Past tense: Ik ...", "answers": ["Ik belde hem op"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Zij nemen een paraplu mee.", "instruction": "Perfect: Zij ...", "answers": ["Zij hebben een paraplu meegenomen", "Ze hebben een paraplu meegenomen"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Hij nodigt ons uit.", "instruction": "Start with: Ik weet dat hij ons ...", "answers": ["Ik weet dat hij ons uitnodigt"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik moet haar opbellen.", "instruction": "Start with: Ik probeer haar ...", "answers": ["Ik probeer haar op te bellen"] },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik bel je morgen op.", "alt": ["Morgen bel ik je op."], "en": "I will call you tomorrow." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Hij is gisteren teruggekomen.", "alt": ["Gisteren is hij teruggekomen."], "en": "He came back yesterday." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik hoop dat hij me morgen opbelt.", "en": "I hope that he will call me tomorrow." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Wij nodigden haar voor het feest uit.", "alt": ["Voor het feest nodigden wij haar uit."], "en": "We invited her to the party." },
